> I think I could deprecate my own Spring Session Manager in favour of Spring's implementation

@mrniko this makes sense to me, and it looks like it will be a quick change for us to switch to Spring’s session repository.

We should note that it’s not quite a drop-in change, because the keys don’t quite align: Spring does [`prefix + ":sessions:" + id`](https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-session/blob/e46610f53ada038194bc262857264e62727e4737/spring-session-data-redis/src/main/java/org/springframework/session/data/redis/RedisIndexedSessionRepository.java#L593), while Redisson does [`prefix + id`](https://github.com/redisson/redisson/blob/287dd1dc416cf300ccfc7ef4952f719549837b85/redisson/src/main/java/org/redisson/spring/session/RedissonSessionRepository.java#L95).
